SamenvattingDo you enjoy being active and like the idea of ​​being part of DHL? Then be sure to read on and discover what this job has to offer. Good work! Over de functieThis role is ideal if you enjoy being active and like variety.
Your responsibilities:
- Sorting and scanning parcels;
- Loading and unloading shipments;
- Working on the conveyor belt;
- Handling parcels of various sizes and weights;
- Supporting efficient daily warehouse operations.

The warehouse worker position involves working in a two-shift system. The working hours are 15:00/17:00-23:00, 17:00-02:30, 23:00-07:00. It is a job for 24–32 hours per week. 
Over het bedrijfYour new employer, DHL, is an essential link in the global logistics process. Packages are sorted, shipped, and delivered in more than 200 countries. You will be working at the Amsterdam location. You will work in a modern environment and be part of a driven and motivated team. 
Wat wij vragenYou have your own accomodation in the Netherlands; 
Good command of the Dutch or English language;
Performing physical work is no problem for you;
You are motivated, work well in a team, and are accurate;
You are available to work flexibly in a two-shift system.

Of course, these points are essential for the role of order picker, but we are primarily interested in who you are! Inspire us.

Wat wij biedenA salary of €14,99 gross per hour;
Shift allowance:125% → from 20:00 to 24:00
130% → from 00:00 to 07:00;

Weekend allowance:+50% on Saturdays
+100% on Sundays

Travel allowance up to €13,80 per day;
Extra money when you work overtime: 150%.

Meer informatieApplying only takes 2 minutes. Do you have any questions? Kamila will be happy to anwser them on:+31625477379 or k.spiewak@carriere.com Good work!

SamenvattingReady to take the next step in logistics? As an Orderpicker you collect orders in a modern distribution center and work alongside a team to keep everything running smoothly. Enjoy a structured work environment, varied tasks, and opportunities to develop your skills. Good work!Over de functieAs an Orderpicker you play an important role in making sure stores and online customers receive their orders on time. You work with a voice-picking system and EPT to collect and prepare products for shipment.

Your tasks:
- Picking orders using a voice-picking system;
- Collecting and preparing products for shipment;
- Scanning and checking items;
- Moving pallets using an EPT;
- Working in ambient, chilled, and frozen warehouse areas.

The work is physically active and involves plenty of walking, lifting and standing throughout your shift. Depending on business needs, you may work in different warehouse departments and temperature zones.
Working hours: 
Dayshift: 08:00–16:00 
Night shifts: 01:00–09:00.
Work is scheduled between Monday and Sunday.
Over het bedrijfYou will be working at a warehouse in Bleiswijk, where groceries are collected and prepared for shipment on a daily basis. Together with your colleagues, you ensure that orders are processed accurately and on time. You will join a diverse team where colleagues help one another and work together to achieve daily goals. 
Wat wij vragen- Own accommodation in The Netherlands. For this job we don't provide housing;
- Working in a cold environment is no problem for you, just like physical work;
- English speaking skills required (voice picking is also available in Dutch and Polish);
- You are available for night shifts, weekends, and national holidays;
- No experience required, just motivation and responsibility 

Of course, these points are essential for the role of order picker, but we are primarily interested in who you are! Inspire us.

Wat wij bieden- A salary starting at €16,20 gross per hour

- Packing and repacking products into cardboard export boxes;
- Preparing creams in a 400-liter mixing tank according to established formulas;
- Operating filling machines for tubes, wound care products, and FFP2 face masks;
- Replenishing raw materials and production supplies;
- Accurately completing production and quality documentation;
- Identifying and resolving minor technical issues;
- Setting up and changing over production lines;
- Supporting warehouse operations when needed;
- Working in accordance with CE, FDA, and cleanroom guidelines;
- Contributing ideas for process improvements and preventing recurring technical issues.

The company places a strong emphasis on independence. You will be trained to operate multiple machines and production stations independently as part of your development within the organization.

- Holds at least a VAPRO A diploma or an equivalent qualification;
- Speaks and writes either Dutch or English;
- Has technical insight and can analyze and solve equipment malfunctions;
- Works accurately, takes responsibility, and can work independently;
- Feels comfortable in an environment where quality standards and procedures are important;
- Brings discipline, energy, and a positive attitude to work.
